*Hals, Wednesday 18 November 2026* {right:*Wind NW 18 m/s · High water 06:52*}
===

## {big:Gale tonight: boats stay in from 20:00}
*Harbour master asks skippers to double their lines before dark; the fuel pier reopens in the morning.*

::: 3
{small:**BY THE HARBOUR OFFICE**}

@dropcap
A northwesterly gale of 18 metres a second is expected to reach Aalborg Bugt this evening, the harbour office said on Wednesday. Boats are asked to stay in from 20:00 until the wind falls below 12 m/s, probably before noon on Thursday.

The warning went out over the new repeater on the mast and reached Øster Hurup in two hops, before the radio forecast mentioned it. "We heard it on the water first," said one skipper.

![The gale building over the harbour mouth on Wednesday afternoon.](demo/storm.png "colour wide")

>! [rules] {big:*"We heard the gale warning on the water before the radio said it."*}
>{small:Anna, skipper of Mågen}

### Fuel pier open again
Diesel and petrol are back at the fuel pier from Thursday 07:00, card only. The pump was out for two weeks while the tank was replaced.

![The fuel pier, open again.](demo/fuelpier.png "colour wide")

{small:**WEATHER · TONIGHT**}
| | Wind | Sea |
|---|---|---|
| Morning | 8 W | calm |
| Afternoon | 14 W | choppy |
| Night | {red:**18 NW**} | {red:**rough**} |

### Repeater covers the bay
The new repeater on the mast now hears nodes across the whole bay. A page like this one takes about twenty seconds over LoRa, and its pictures come when you tap them.

![Chart of the bay, drawn in dots: sharp at 2 KB.](demo/demo-chart.png "dots wide")

Readers who want to test their antenna can write their signal strength in the classifieds below; the harbour office collects the numbers for a coverage map.
:::

